This, I think, is where a lot of people kill ascendable characters;
getting fixated on a particular problem and trying to solve it _right
then_, even if it means doing it the hard way or a really complex way
that requires a lot of careful attention.

Nethack is, in many ways, not so much about solving problems as it is
about obviating them completely, so that they require no attention.  
The troll with a wand of death is either a problem to be solved (if 
you insist on killing him now) or moot (if you go for the Castle and 
